timestamps are exactly the twins results
1	1	1
2	1	1
3	1	1
the step decides which capture a row satisfying both conditions carries
{"id":3,"sequenceMatchEventsAllWithCapture('(?1)(?2)')(t, bitTest(e, 0), bitTest(e, 1), CAST(map('as', 'view'), 'JSON'), CAST(map('as', 'purchase'), 'JSON'))":[[{"t":0,"capture":{"as":"view"}},{"t":5,"capture":{"as":"purchase"}}]],"sequenceMatchEventsAllWithCapture('(?2)')(t, bitTest(e, 0), bitTest(e, 1), CAST(map('as', 'view'), 'JSON'), CAST(map('as', 'purchase'), 'JSON'))":[[{"t":5,"capture":{"as":"purchase"}}]]}
Nullable(JSON) captures, NULL on some rows
{"sequenceMatchEventsAllWithCapture('(?1).*(?2)')(t, bitTest(e, 0), bitTest(e, 1), if(greater(price, 9), CAST(map('v', product), 'JSON'), NULL), CAST(map('p', product), 'JSON'))":[[{"t":0,"capture":{"v":"shoes"}},{"t":7,"capture":{"p":"hat"}}],[{"t":20,"capture":{"v":"bag"}},{"t":22,"capture":{"p":"bag"}}]]}
result types
Array(Array(Tuple(\n    t UInt32,\n    capture Nullable(JSON))))
Array(Tuple(\n    t Date,\n    capture Nullable(JSON)))
Array(Tuple(\n    t UInt64,\n    capture Nullable(JSON(a UInt8))))
DateTime timestamps
{"sequenceMatchEventsWithCapture('(?1)(?t>=86400&&t<=604800)(?2)')(ts, equals(e, 1), equals(e, 2), CAST(map('step', 'view'), 'JSON'), CAST(map('step', 'buy'), 'JSON'))":[{"t":"2026-01-01 00:00:00","capture":{"step":"view"}},{"t":"2026-01-03 00:00:00","capture":{"step":"buy"}}]}
